        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-12T15:41:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this needed in the backend API?  The PDC driver API already provides a mechanism to read the cable property.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 434,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "8a5b45b487d8d02359698aa47cb684a826769c44",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95320ec5_ab1abe86",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/emul_pdc.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1531252
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-12T16:40:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general I prefer directly exposing the corresponding emulator properties/functions even when they correspond to a driver function. This allows for tests that give a clearer signal if something is wrong specifically in the emulator vs something being wrong in the PDC subsystem or in the I2C layer. Eventually I think we\u0027d want to move toward an architecture where we\u0027d be attaching some sort of cable object to the emulator instead of directly touching emulator properties and a function like this would help facilitate testing since that would something specific to the emulator.",
      "parentUuid": "fa9e70ac_80d141b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 434,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "8a5b45b487d8d02359698aa47cb684a826769c44",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "145b8e6b_175caebd",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/emul/emul_pdc.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-12T16:48:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to attaching an abstracted cable/partner object as the backend operation instead of having the test directly specify the cable property.\n\nI understand your point about failure isolation, but I don\u0027t agree that it\u0027s necessary. I prefer to keep the backend API surface small so that the tests are easier to follow.  The goal is to provide coverate of the real driver/subsystem code.  This kind of isolation just serves as a unit test of the emulator",
      "parentUuid": "95320ec5_ab1abe86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 434,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "8a5b45b487d8d02359698aa47cb684a826769c44",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b57e4d8f_8846d20a",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/generic/pdc_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 375,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-12T15:41:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems unnecessary.  This is effectively just testing the emulator code, but the `pdc_get_cable_property()` call should also verify the emulator is populating the cable property data.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 372,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 375,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "8a5b45b487d8d02359698aa47cb684a826769c44",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfaa51d7_0d02f008",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/pdc/src/generic/pdc_api.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 375,
